# Each building holds eight sends. Keys 1-8 send from the building selected on the command card.
# "inc" is income PER ROUND (classic and quick pay income once when a round ends). 0.18 send table: the
# income rate (inc / cost, per round) rises smoothly with the price across ALL buildings, from 3.3 % for the
# 30 g sends to 6.0 % for the Void Colossus (target curve: 3 % x 2^u, u = log-position of the price between
# 30 and 2600 g; incomes are whole numbers, so the cheap end sits on a 3.33 % plateau and the rate never falls
# as the price rises). The counterweights (see Sim): the cheap sends carry ~1.4x more pressure per gold
# (health x damage for the price) and their killer is paid about half as much of their price as the dear
# ones' (Sim.send_gift_k). The buildings' prices gate the better rates; there is no per-round income cap
# any more. Power sends (the last two of each building) keep their 0.17 income costs: they are priced
# against a player's income, not the table. The 10 s modes (survival, tutorial, campaign) read the table
# through Sim.send_inc, which divides by Sim.INC_UNIT and pays at least +1 a tick.
